Tiled CPU flash attention (ggml_compute_forward_flash_attn_ext_tiled, used for 64+ query rows with F16 / F32 K and V):
pack each 64-row K tile (transposed, F16 -> F32) and V tile (F16 -> F32) once for up to GGML_FA_TILE_NQ = 4
consecutive 64-row Q tiles of the same head, instead of once per Q tile. Each Q row still goes through the same
operations in the same order (same KV tile order, same GEMM, scale, max, softmax and V accumulation), so the
output is bit-identical. GGML_CPU_FA_KV_REUSE=0 packs per Q tile again (the old schedule).
Per-thread scratch goes from 160 KiB to 448 KiB at DK = DV = 128.

